---
import LegalPage from '../../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site.js';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Haiyun Grain Machine collects, uses, shares and retains enquiry and website data, including international transfers, cookies and your privacy rights."
  lede="This policy explains what personal data we receive when you use this website or contact our team, why we use it, and the choices available to you."
>
  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    The website <a href={site.url}>{site.url}</a> is operated by {site.legalName}, a company
    located at {site.address.full}. For the purposes of applicable data-protection law, {site.legalName}
    is the controller of the personal data described in this policy.
  </p>
  <p>
    Privacy contact: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. Telephone:
    {site.phone}. Business hours: {site.hours}. We do not currently appoint a statutory
    data-protection officer; privacy requests are handled by the address above.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Scope</h2>
  <p>
    This policy covers personal data collected through this website, by email, telephone,
    WhatsApp or other direct business communication, and during the preparation or performance
    of a commercial project. It does not cover third-party websites we link to, or the separate
    privacy practices of distributors and service providers.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Personal data we collect</h2>
  <p>We collect only what is needed to answer an enquiry and manage a business relationship:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Contact details:</strong> name, company, job title, country, email address, telephone or WhatsApp number.</li>
    <li><strong>Enquiry details:</strong> wheat specification, target capacity, site constraints, drawings, photographs, project timeline and correspondence.</li>
    <li><strong>Commercial records:</strong> quotations, contracts, invoices, shipping documents and warranty records where a project proceeds.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical website data:</strong> IP address, browser type, requested page, time of request and basic server logs generated by our hosting provider.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not require an account to read the site. We do not collect payment-card details through
    the website; payments are handled by bank transfer against a formal contract.
  </p>

  <h2>4. How and why we use personal data</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Data used</th><th>Legal basis (where GDPR/UK GDPR applies)</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Answer an enquiry and prepare a technical proposal</td><td>Contact and enquiry details</td><td>Steps at your request before a contract; our legitimate interest in responding to B2B enquiries</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Perform a contract, arrange shipping and provide after-sales support</td><td>Contact, commercial and project records</td><td>Performance of a contract</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Keep accounting, tax, warranty and compliance records</td><td>Commercial records</td><td>Legal obligation; legitimate interest in defending legal claims</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Protect the website and prevent abuse</td><td>Technical logs</td><td>Legitimate interest in network and information security</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Send marketing communications</td><td>Business contact details</td><td>Consent where required; otherwise the soft opt-in or legitimate interest permitted by law</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Where we rely on legitimate interests, we consider whether the processing is necessary and
    whether your rights override those interests. You may object at any time using the contact
    details below.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Cookies and third-party requests</h2>
  <p>
    This website does not set advertising or analytics cookies and does not run advertising
    networks. It loads web fonts from Google Fonts, which means your browser connects to Google's
    servers and your IP address is visible to Google. See our
    <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a> for the full list and browser controls.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Sharing</h2>
  <p>We do not sell, rent or trade personal data. We may share it with:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>our sales, engineering, quality and finance staff who need it for the project;</li>
    <li>authorised overseas representatives, where one covers your territory and the project requires local support;</li>
    <li>hosting, email, freight, inspection and professional advisers acting under appropriate confidentiality terms;</li>
    <li>courts, regulators or authorities where disclosure is required by law or necessary to establish, exercise or defend legal claims.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Our operations are based in China. If you contact us from the European Economic Area, the
    United Kingdom, Switzerland or another jurisdiction with transfer rules, your data may be
    transferred to and processed in China. We use the transfer mechanism required by applicable
    law — for example contractual safeguards, a legal necessity or your explicit consent where
    consent is the applicable basis — and apply the protections described in this policy.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where the PRC Personal Information Protection Law applies, we process personal data for the
    purposes stated here and take steps required for cross-border transfer. You may contact us for
    information about the safeguards used for your data.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Retention</h2>
  <p>
    Enquiry records are normally retained for up to 24 months after the last contact. If an enquiry
    becomes a contract, project, invoice or warranty record, the relevant records may be retained
    for the period required for accounting, tax, warranty, export-control and legal purposes —
    typically up to seven years, or longer where a legal obligation or dispute requires it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Website server logs are retained only for the period needed for security and troubleshooting,
    unless a longer period is required to investigate abuse.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Security</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served over HTTPS. Enquiry and project data are stored in access-controlled systems,
    with access limited to staff and advisers who need it. We do not accept card details through the
    website. No internet transmission is completely secure; if you believe your data has been
    compromised, contact us immediately.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on your location, you may have the right to access, correct, delete, restrict or
    object to processing, to receive a portable copy of your data, or to withdraw consent. To make a
    request, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> with the subject
    “Data request”. We normally respond within 30 days and may ask for information needed to verify
    your identity.
  </p>
  <p>
    You may also complain to your local data-protection authority. In the UK, this is the
    Information Commissioner's Office; in an EU member state, the supervisory authority in your
    country of residence or work. If you are in China, you may contact the relevant
    personal-information protection authority.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Children</h2>
  <p>
    This is a business-to-business engineering website. It is not directed at children and we do
    not knowingly collect personal data from anyone under 16. If you believe a child has provided
    data, contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Automated decisions</h2>
  <p>
    We do not use automated decision-making that produces legal or similarly significant effects
    about you. Enquiries are reviewed by our commercial and engineering staff.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy when our practices or legal requirements change. The revised version
    will be posted here with a new “Last updated” date. Material changes will be communicated where
    required by law.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    {site.legalName}<br />
    {site.address.full}<br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a><br />
    Telephone: {site.phone}
  </p>
</LegalPage>
